;; The datetime differential corpus: every KNOWN divergence from a real
;; PostgreSQL, one entry per sample. Generated by
;;   (datahike.fuzz.differential/run-surface :datetime 0 0)
;; and intended to BURN DOWN to the carrier entries alone.
;;
;; A divergence NOT listed here fails `bb fuzz datetime`. A listed
;; one that now agrees also fails, with BASELINE DRIFT -- so a fix
;; is not complete until its entries are pruned from this file.
;;
;; Two reasons appear:
;;   PARSER:  the three regexes standing in for ParseDateTime and
;;            DecodeDateTime/DecodeTimeOnly. The port removes these.
;;   CARRIER: java.util.Date is millisecond precision. The port does
;;            NOT remove these; they need a different carrier.
;;
;; WHICH PostgreSQL: this baseline was generated against the LOCAL
;; oracle, which is 17.10, while CI pins cimg/postgres:17.7. I wrote
;; "17.7" when I committed it and that was wrong. datetime.c is very
;; unlikely to differ across a patch release, and that is now CHECKED
;; rather than assumed: CI ran this manifest against 17.7 and reported
;; neither an unexpected divergence nor a baseline drift, so all 670
;; samples behave identically on the two releases.
;;
;; Baseline 2026-10-03: 239 of 670 samples diverge.

